15 0 obj
<< /A 35 0 R /Alt (Two Kaplan-Meier survival curves comparing head/neck cancers to other locations. Graph A shows overall survival probability over 60 months, with a significant p-value of 0.025. Graph B illustrates disease-free survival over the same period with a p-value of 0.017. Both graphs indicate higher survival probabilities in non-head/neck locations.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 28 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
16 0 obj
<< /A 36 0 R /Alt (Diagram of a human body, front and back view, annotated with survival statistics. Head and neck: 51.6% OS, 45.3% DFS. Upper limbs: 72.7% OS, 67.5% DFS. Torso: 60.3% OS, 51.6% DFS. Buttocks: 51.5% OS, 51.5% DFS. Lower limbs: 63.5% OS, 60.4% DFS. OS refers to overall survival; DFS refers to disease-free survival.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 29 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
17 0 obj
<< /A 37 0 R /Alt (Two Kaplan-Meier survival curves comparing head/neck and other locations. Graph A shows overall survival probability against time in months, with a p-value of 0.005. Graph B shows disease-free survival probability with a p-value of 0.004. Both graphs indicate a higher survival probability for other locations compared to head/neck. Number at risk is listed for each interval.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 30 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
